<section id="apology">
<div class="eyebrow center">First, something I owe you</div>
<h2>I'm truly sorry.</h2>
<p class="section-intro">
Before I remind you of all the beautiful things I love about us,
I want to acknowledge the hurt I caused you. You deserve that honesty first.
</p>
<div class="paper">
<div class="letter">
<p>My Hritikaaa,</p>
<p>
I have been thinking about what my actions put you through, and I don't
want this apology to become another attempt to explain myself. I want to
take the time to acknowledge what happened and, more importantly, what
it must have felt like for you.
</p>
<p>
I replied to someone from my past while I was already in a relationship
with you. I allowed that conversation to become personal. I hid it from
you, and when you asked me about it, I lied to you twice. I know that
writing these things plainly does not undo them, but I owe you the truth
without making it smaller or more comfortable for myself.
</p>
<p>
I understand that this was never just about a message. It was about the
person you trusted making a choice that made you question where you stood.
It may have made you wonder whether you were truly being chosen, whether
there was still someone else occupying a place in my life, and whether
you could trust what I told you. You should never have been made to feel
that you had to compete with my past.
</p>
<p>
You should not have had to discover things instead of hearing the truth
from me. You should not have had to ask repeatedly for honesty. And you
should not have been left carrying the emotional weight of trying to
understand, process and repair something that my actions damaged.
</p>
<p>
I also understand that my explanations can feel like I am defending
myself instead of listening to you. I don't want to do that anymore.
Whatever I was feeling at the time does not erase the impact of what
I chose to do. My intentions cannot cancel out your experience.
</p>
<p>
I am sorry for the hurt, the uncertainty, the anger and the exhaustion
that followed. I am sorry for the moments when you felt alone in a
relationship where you deserved honesty, consideration and emotional
security. I am sorry that someone who should have protected your trust
became the reason you had to question it.
</p>
<p>
I don't expect you to forget this, get over it quickly, or trust me
simply because I have written a heartfelt letter. You have every right
to have questions, to need time, and to feel differently on different
days. I want to listen without becoming defensive, even when the
conversation is uncomfortable for me.
</p>
<p>
I need to show change in the things I do: being honest even when the
truth is difficult, maintaining clear boundaries with people from my
past, never hiding conversations, and being consistent rather than
only making promises when things are falling apart.
</p>
<p>
You deserve a relationship where you don't have to keep searching for
reassurance or wondering whether the truth is being withheld. I want
to become someone whose actions make honesty feel dependable again.
I know that is something I have to demonstrate over time.
</p>
<p>
I am not asking you to make my guilt feel lighter. I am asking you to
know that I recognise the hurt I caused, that I take responsibility
for it, and that I want to do the work without placing that responsibility
on you.
</p>
<p>
You mattered then. You matter now. And you deserved better from me
than what I gave you in those moments.
</p>
<p class="signature">With all my love, and with genuine remorse.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="rule"></div>
